+### N3. ⚪ `skip-entra=1` opts one `/init` out of drop2
+
+**Where:** `auth-handover.drop2.entra.js` (`beginFromInit` → `_skipRequested`, reason
+`skip-entra-requested`), reached from this feature's `appAuthRedirect`.
+**Test:** `auth-handover.drop2.entra.unit.test.js` → "skip-entra=1 …".
+
+A caller that finds a live CMS session with a `<script>` tag (JSONP to
+`/auth-refresh-termination?cb=…`, as polaris-ui's in-situ reauth does) cannot follow drop2's
+silent Entra round trip: Entra answers `prompt=none` with an HTML page, which the browser
+refuses as a script (`ERR_BLOCKED_BY_ORB`), so a live session reads as "failed to load".
+With `skip-entra=1`, `/init` carries on exactly as with Entra off and logs a `skipped` outcome
+with reason `skip-entra-requested`. Only exactly `1` counts.
+
+The arg reaches `/init` from every entry: `/auth-refresh-outbound` forwards its whole query
+string, the proxied `/polaris` clones its args, and the real CMS `/polaris` forwards extra args
+(as it does `terminal=iframe`). It changes nothing a user could not already get: drop2 is
+best-effort and every failure carries on the same way. The handover that follows a successful
+probe goes through `/init` without the flag, so the MDS deposit still happens then.
